  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;be the equation of a curve, then the <math><mi>x</mi></math>-intercept of the tangent to this curve whose slope is least, is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>≥</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />So, minimum value is <math><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math> when <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />Hence, equation of tangent is <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math><br />So,&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi></math> -intercept <math><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
